        {
          "name": "Resistant",
          "type": "ex",
          "description": "A metal cactuar is unusually resistant to everything, gaining a +5 resistance bonus to all saving throws.",
          "notes": {
            "familiar": ""
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Thorns",
          "type": "ex",
          "description": "A metal cactuar's body is covered with sharp metal thorns. Any creature attacking a metal cactuar with a non-reach melee weapon or with natural attacks takes 1d4+2 points of piercing damage from the metal cactuar's sharp thorns. A creature that grapples with a metal cactuar takes this same damage each round.",
          "notes": {
            "familiar": ""
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Thousand Needles",
          "type": "su",
          "description": "3/day, a metal cactuar may conjure up a spray of needles and fires them at targets in a 30-ft.-cone. Creatures within the area take 8d4 points of piercing damage (Reflex save DC 14 for half damage). Blue mages may learn this ability as a 3rd level spell (Knowledge: Nature DC 21).",
          "notes": {
            "familiar": ""
          }
        }
      ],
      "description": "This creature appears to be a small cactus made entirely out of metal, having physical characteristics similar to a humanoid: two arms, two legs and dark spots on its anterior in the shape of a mouth and eyes. Its limbs protrude and bend at ninety-degree angles giving it a rigid look, which belies the speed and agility with which it can move. - Imban"
